abstract: >-
  A speculative hypothesis treating the universe as a globally conserved
  informational structure, where cosmological cycles correspond to changes in
  local information readability rather than temporal restarts. Version 0.1.6
  adds a fixed-dimension restricted-entropy stability bound and a bounded
  review of prescribed observable-algebra transport. It clarifies why mass
  inaccessibility does not establish conformal invariance and why gravitational
  entropy comparisons require consistent calibration and horizon accounting.
  Earlier selector and measurement results are unchanged. Neither the bound
  nor the transport construction supplies a physical algebra selector, a
  cosmological entropy functional, transition dynamics, or predictions.
